Seeker: Oh, yeah, we had some once.

02:26:40.812 --> 02:26:41.092
DM: It's the-

02:26:41.112 --> 02:26:41.472
Unknown: Yeah

02:26:41.472 --> 02:26:46.032
DM: ... metal you had. It's what power, well, it's what holds the binding stone...

02:26:46.032 --> 02:26:46.852
DM: Or sorry, the-

02:26:46.892 --> 02:26:47.712
Seeker: The phasing stone

02:26:47.712 --> 02:26:48.332
DM: ... phasing stone in place.

02:26:48.372 --> 02:26:48.872
Unknown: Yeah.

02:26:48.872 --> 02:26:56.132
DM: Yeah. And he's like tracing with his hand, and as he does, um, letters appear on this like thin sheet of this metal.

02:26:56.132 --> 02:27:01.152
DM: And then he puts the dagger down and he like wraps the metal around it and he starts beating it again.

02:27:01.152 --> 02:27:02.172
DM: This goes on for,

02:27:03.572 --> 02:27:09.792
DM: you know, a while. It seems like he's just doing layer after layer where he's putting some spells on it and then beating something into the dagger.

02:27:10.832 --> 02:27:14.172
DM: And then the scene shifts, and it seems

02:27:15.672 --> 02:27:17.132
DM: some time later,

02:27:18.852 --> 02:27:22.212
DM: and there is, um, like you can't quite...

02:27:22.212 --> 02:27:26.992
DM: You can't see what it is, but there's clearly a person chained in the manacles.

02:27:26.992 --> 02:27:29.032
DM: But your, your perspective is looking down-

02:27:29.032 --> 02:27:29.312
Unknown: Yeah, so you-

02:27:29.312 --> 02:27:31.952
DM: ... at the manacles, so you basically just see wrists.

02:27:31.952 --> 02:27:40.892
DM: And then the wrists go limp and you can see like slashes, the dagger slashing the wrists, and the blood

02:27:42.292 --> 02:27:47.832
DM: runs down into the floor, like running down the arms.

02:27:47.832 --> 02:27:48.152
DM: But

02:27:49.212 --> 02:27:59.452
DM: there's some like spark that runs into the dagger from the manacles, and this happens again and again, and the floor now you can see this like well in the middle is filling

02:27:59.452 --> 02:28:02.772
DM: up with blood of like 10 people.

02:28:03.172 --> 02:28:03.492
Unknown: Oh, God.

02:28:03.492 --> 02:28:08.412
DM: And it gets... It's drying out and it gets darker and thicker as it dries out.

02:28:09.532 --> 02:28:15.452
DM: And the mirror shifts again, and you can see now Apollyon standing.

02:28:15.452 --> 02:28:21.132
DM: The manacle's empty, and he is kneeling on the floor.

02:28:21.132 --> 02:28:28.232
DM: The blood all dried except for in this very well in the very center, which now looks black, and he draws a

02:28:29.352 --> 02:28:36.272
DM: clear vial, like a potion vial out from his, from his robes, and he begins...

02:28:36.272 --> 02:28:42.192
DM: The, the, the gems in the crown, there's like shadow flowing out of the crown into the blood.

02:28:42.192 --> 02:28:52.212
DM: It begins to swirl, and this sort of dark black viscous liquid floats up and pours itself into the vial, which he then

02:28:52.212 --> 02:28:52.852
DM: stoppers.

02:28:54.772 --> 02:28:59.672
DM: And Seeker recalls that the lore of licks is typically that they are...

02:29:00.712 --> 02:29:08.992
DM: To become a lick you need to create a phylactery, and then you need to make a potion somehow, the rituals are not known, from

02:29:10.392 --> 02:29:14.152
DM: involving somehow the souls of the people who fed your phylactery.

02:29:14.152 --> 02:29:14.872
Delwath: It's the dagger.

02:29:14.892 --> 02:29:18.172
DM: And when you drink the potion, you turn into a lick.

02:29:19.492 --> 02:29:21.412
DM: But the dagger is clearly the phylactery.

02:29:22.632 --> 02:29:25.072
DM: Plain, unadorned-

02:29:25.092 --> 02:29:25.112
Unknown: Hm

02:29:25.112 --> 02:29:26.712
DM: ... uninteresting dagger.

02:29:26.712 --> 02:29:30.032
DM: The only notable fact is its blade is made out of adamantine.

02:29:30.792 --> 02:29:33.372
Delwath: Seeker can find adamantine, can't he?

02:29:33.372 --> 02:29:35.012
Seeker: That's a good point.

02:29:35.012 --> 02:29:35.812
DM: I believe he can.

02:29:36.392 --> 02:29:38.132
Delwath: Yeah, it's probably not that common of a metal.

02:29:39.352 --> 02:29:40.152
DM: Possibly not.

02:29:40.412 --> 02:29:41.912
Seeker: No. It's... No, it's not.

02:29:42.792 --> 02:29:43.832
Kenzo: How do you find adamantine?

02:29:44.692 --> 02:29:46.432
Seeker: Well, I have my stone sense, which can-

02:29:46.452 --> 02:29:47.532
Kenzo: What's the range?

02:29:47.532 --> 02:29:49.912
DM: 1,000 feet, so it's not super wide.

02:29:50.192 --> 02:29:50.432
Unknown: Yeah.

02:29:50.952 --> 02:29:52.272
Kenzo: But you can amplify that with your, uh-

02:29:52.412 --> 02:29:53.572
Seeker: No, that's not for spells I think

02:29:54.772 --> 02:29:54.812
Unknown: ...

02:29:55.912 --> 02:29:56.132
Unknown: amplifier.

02:29:56.152 --> 02:29:56.372
DM: Um, yeah.

02:29:56.372 --> 02:29:56.692
Unknown: The glyph.

02:29:56.692 --> 02:30:03.652
DM: Well, and that's... So that's a spell that targets the range itself, and it gives you an ability to sense 1,000 feet.

02:30:06.152 --> 02:30:06.292
DM: So you-

02:30:06.292 --> 02:30:08.672
Delwath: You can only increase where the range of the spell.

02:30:08.672 --> 02:30:10.532
Delwath: You can't increase the range of-

02:30:10.572 --> 02:30:10.572
DM: Right

02:30:10.572 --> 02:30:12.732
Delwath: ... the effect of a spell that you cast on yourself.

02:30:12.772 --> 02:30:13.172
DM: Right.

02:30:13.252 --> 02:30:13.732
Unknown: Oh, okay.

02:30:13.732 --> 02:30:15.832
Wellby: You couldn't double the radius of a fireball.

02:30:15.912 --> 02:30:16.072
DM: Yeah.

02:30:16.092 --> 02:30:16.372
Unknown: Right.

02:30:16.392 --> 02:30:18.292
DM: You couldn't... Like a fireball's a 20-foot radius.

02:30:18.312 --> 02:30:19.332
DM: You couldn't make it 40 feet.

02:30:19.372 --> 02:30:20.932
Delwath: But you could make it appear-

02:30:20.932 --> 02:30:22.052
DM: You could make it appear farther away

02:30:22.052 --> 02:30:22.932
Delwath: ... farther away.

02:30:22.972 --> 02:30:23.212
DM: Right.

02:30:26.852 --> 02:30:27.252
Unknown: All right.

02:30:27.352 --> 02:30:27.712
Delwath: All right.

02:30:28.092 --> 02:30:28.312
Wellby: Okay.

02:30:28.392 --> 02:30:28.812
Unknown: I mean-

02:30:28.852 --> 02:30:30.672
Wellby: Have we ever seen this dagger before?

02:30:31.912 --> 02:30:32.572
DM: I mean,

02:30:33.732 --> 02:30:36.832
DM: you've seen hundreds of daggers that look very similar to it, right?

02:30:36.832 --> 02:30:37.972
DM: Like part of the...

02:30:39.252 --> 02:30:43.752
DM: It's clear that part of the design is to make it look as uninteresting as possible.

02:30:43.952 --> 02:30:44.092
Unknown: Right.

02:30:44.172 --> 02:30:45.472
DM: It just looks like a normal dagger.

02:30:45.732 --> 02:30:49.792
Seeker: Well, 1,000 feet of stone sense would cover the entirety of the tower that we're in now.

02:30:49.792 --> 02:30:51.512
Seeker: It's probably not here though.

02:30:51.531 --> 02:30:51.692
Unknown: No, no.

02:30:51.752 --> 02:30:52.472
Delwath: No, it's more Drankorian.

02:30:52.512 --> 02:30:53.771
Kenzo: It's Drankorian.

02:30:53.771 --> 02:30:53.892
Unknown: But-

02:30:53.892 --> 02:30:55.711
Delwath: 'Cause 1,000 feet in all directions.

02:30:55.752 --> 02:30:55.952
DM: Yep.

02:30:57.132 --> 02:30:59.512
Kenzo: I mean, it would be ridiculous if it were literally here and we could kill

02:31:00.572 --> 02:31:01.672
Unknown: Apollyon right now.

02:31:01.712 --> 02:31:03.072
Delwath: I mean, is your stone sense a free action?

02:31:04.152 --> 02:31:04.252
Unknown: I mean-

02:31:04.272 --> 02:31:06.512
Unknown: It's just a spell. It's like an action.

02:31:06.512 --> 02:31:07.472
Delwath: But I mean, how many times-

02:31:07.512 --> 02:31:08.352
DM: And so you, you just hold up the ring and-

02:31:08.352 --> 02:31:09.492
Delwath: How many times can you do it?

02:31:09.772 --> 02:31:10.492
DM: Three times a day.

02:31:10.532 --> 02:31:11.152
Seeker: Three times a day, yeah.

02:31:11.172 --> 02:31:13.572
Delwath: You, you may as well see if there's any adamantine in this tower.

02:31:13.612 --> 02:31:14.572
Seeker: I'm gonna just do that. I will just right now.

02:31:14.572 --> 02:31:15.332
Delwath: Right? Like what's the harm?

02:31:18.372 --> 02:31:20.252
Seeker: Um, here, I'll pull up the stone sense.

02:31:21.332 --> 02:31:24.412
Kenzo: Do we have any sense of when the... So he was 50 years old, so he w- this would've been like-

02:31:24.452 --> 02:31:27.752
DM: This was probably tw- close towards the end of his reign.

02:31:28.892 --> 02:31:28.932
Unknown: Okay.

02:31:28.932 --> 02:31:32.512
DM: Like not at the very last moment, but within the last 10 years.

02:31:32.552 --> 02:31:35.452
Kenzo: Yeah, 'cause he was in civil war with Shemut, or he was in conflict with Shemut.

02:31:35.472 --> 02:31:36.472
DM: He, yeah, he was in conflict with Shemut.

02:31:36.492 --> 02:31:40.532
Kenzo: And probably know that it was not going well 'cause Shemut like was about to wipe him out and put him in prison.

02:31:42.412 --> 02:31:43.132
DM: Do you want to sense it?

02:31:43.852 --> 02:31:45.232
Seeker: I will use stone sense to-

02:31:45.312 --> 02:31:47.632
DM: Okay

02:31:47.632 --> 02:31:49.472
Seeker: ... search for adamantine.

02:31:49.592 --> 02:31:52.552
DM: Okay. There are, there is adamantine.

02:31:52.552 --> 02:31:54.532
DM: There's scraps of it on the floor in front of you.

02:31:55.452 --> 02:31:56.572
DM: That's the only adamantine in the tower.

02:31:56.592 --> 02:31:57.452
Unknown: Yeah, that makes sense.

02:31:58.472 --> 02:31:58.572
Unknown: Wow.

02:31:58.592 --> 02:32:01.792
Seeker: Just verifying. Well, that was a good use of the mirror I think, everybody.

02:32:01.832 --> 02:32:02.592
Unknown: That was, that was-

02:32:02.652 --> 02:32:02.812
DM: Oh, yeah. Excellent. [laughs]

02:32:02.812 --> 02:32:04.272
Kenzo: That, that was, that, that was one of the best.

02:32:04.312 --> 02:32:05.892
Seeker: We learned something absolutely crucial.

02:32:05.932 --> 02:32:08.692
Kenzo: That was, that was, that was one of the most important uses ever.

02:32:08.712 --> 02:32:10.992
Unknown: All right, so downward, right?

02:32:11.412 --> 02:32:13.072
Kenzo: Do you want to take the scraps of adamantine?

02:32:13.132 --> 02:32:14.692
Delwath: I mean, you may as well. Honestly.

02:32:14.692 --> 02:32:16.292
Seeker: They, they might be tiny, tiny fragments.

02:32:16.532 --> 02:32:16.832
Unknown: Yeah.

02:32:16.872 --> 02:32:18.112
DM: Yeah, you could gather up like-

02:32:18.292 --> 02:32:19.252
Delwath: But like-

02:32:19.252 --> 02:32:20.652
DM: ... half a pound or something.

02:32:20.752 --> 02:32:20.912
Unknown: Oh.

02:32:20.932 --> 02:32:21.452
Wellby: That's significant.

02:32:21.492 --> 02:32:23.192
Kenzo: But isn't this also useful for some other shit?

02:32:23.192 --> 02:32:25.632
Kenzo: 'Cause like now 'cause it's part of the same adamantine as the dagger so-

02:32:25.652 --> 02:32:26.232
Delwath: I was just gonna say like-

02:32:26.232 --> 02:32:27.832
Kenzo: ... can you like teleport to it or like... You know what I mean?

02:32:28.172 --> 02:32:28.272
Unknown: Like-

02:32:28.292 --> 02:32:28.472
Wellby: Yeah.

02:32:28.512 --> 02:32:29.372
Kenzo: Is there some weird like-

02:32:29.392 --> 02:32:30.272
DM: Yeah, I didn't think of that

02:32:30.272 --> 02:32:33.752
Delwath: ... like there's all kinds of potential abilities.

02:32:33.752 --> 02:32:35.212
Delwath: Like who knows what it is right now, but it's-

02:32:35.232 --> 02:32:35.652
Unknown: Yeah, definitely save this

02:32:35.652 --> 02:32:37.432
Unknown: ... good to have.

02:32:37.472 --> 02:32:41.532
Kenzo: Adamantine scraps from, from, uh, Apollyon's phylactery feels like a useful item.

02:32:41.532 --> 02:32:41.992
DM: [laughs]

02:32:42.132 --> 02:32:42.272
Unknown: Yeah.

02:32:42.632 --> 02:32:42.792
Wellby: Yep.

02:32:43.752 --> 02:32:45.152
Delwath: What if we showed them to the mirror?

02:32:46.572 --> 02:32:48.012
Delwath: But we can't. I know we can't, right?

02:32:48.052 --> 02:32:50.992
DM: I mean, you'd probably just see a worse version of what you just saw.

02:32:51.012 --> 02:32:51.292
Unknown: Right, we probably would.

02:32:51.292 --> 02:32:53.392
DM: You'd see the forging, but not what happened later.

02:32:53.632 --> 02:32:54.532
Seeker: I will add those to my-

02:32:55.172 --> 02:32:55.312
DM: Yeah

02:32:55.312 --> 02:32:57.112
Seeker: ... inventory so we don't forget.

02:32:58.152 --> 02:32:59.872
Wellby: All right, this was definitely worth coming to.

02:33:00.732 --> 02:33:01.352
Unknown: Let's go down.

02:33:02.492 --> 02:33:03.592
DM: Descend the stairs.

02:33:04.212 --> 02:33:05.892
Wellby: Wellby scouting carefully, alertly.

02:33:05.932 --> 02:33:09.092
Kenzo: And, and now we, we just like leave if we feel it's really threatened at all.

02:33:10.032 --> 02:33:10.692
Unknown: Or do we just...

02:33:11.072 --> 02:33:12.012
Wellby: Just gotta move stuff.

02:33:12.012 --> 02:33:13.612
Delwath: I mean, the treasure, right? The treasure.

02:33:13.612 --> 02:33:14.132
Kenzo: Yeah, there's, there's, there's-

02:33:14.132 --> 02:33:14.992
Delwath: Think of the treasure.

02:33:14.992 --> 02:33:20.752
Kenzo: Of course, of course. Well, 'cause the other thing too is this is where he made the, um, made, uh, his flappy.

02:33:20.772 --> 02:33:20.772
Unknown: Yeah.

02:33:20.812 --> 02:33:22.352
Kenzo: But where the fuck did he make the scepter?

02:33:22.352 --> 02:33:23.352
Kenzo: And where else did he make the crown?

02:33:23.432 --> 02:33:24.732
Delwath: That's what I mean by divine forge.

02:33:24.732 --> 02:33:25.072
Unknown: 'Cause that's also definitely where it is.

02:33:25.092 --> 02:33:25.932
Wellby: It's not in this room, yeah.

02:33:25.952 --> 02:33:26.932
Delwath: Yeah, it's probably not in this room.

02:33:27.112 --> 02:33:27.272
Wellby: All right.

02:33:27.272 --> 02:33:27.572
Unknown: It's down.

02:33:27.612 --> 02:33:28.992
DM: The stairs go...

02:33:28.992 --> 02:33:29.872
DM: Make a perception check.

02:33:31.332 --> 02:33:32.392
Wellby: Uh, 23.

02:33:32.772 --> 02:33:40.132
DM: Okay. The stairs go down the entire length of the spire with no breaks or stops or doors.

02:33:40.172 --> 02:33:41.332
Kenzo: Can't you detect underground stuff?

02:33:42.672 --> 02:33:43.052
Unknown: Yes.

02:33:44.212 --> 02:33:45.412
Wellby: Okay.

02:33:45.412 --> 02:33:48.991
Wellby: So this whole second spire is just a room and a very long flight of stairs.

02:33:49.212 --> 02:33:49.552
DM: Yes.

02:33:50.592 --> 02:33:51.432
Delwath: All right, so we come out-

02:33:51.552 --> 02:33:52.332
DM: That's it

02:33:52.332 --> 02:33:54.452
Delwath: ... we come out on the, like, middle section.

02:33:54.452 --> 02:33:55.772
DM: You come out in the middle section.

02:33:56.572 --> 02:33:57.832
DM: There is a, there is a, uh...

02:33:58.552 --> 02:34:04.172
DM: So you come out to a landing that has a door out to the middle section and then more stairs that go down.

02:34:05.312 --> 02:34:06.712
Delwath: And is the door, like, out...

02:34:07.212 --> 02:34:08.112
Delwath: Is it this door?

02:34:08.112 --> 02:34:09.512
DM: It's that door. Yeah, yeah, yeah.

02:34:09.512 --> 02:34:15.692
DM: So, like, you're at a landing where you could exit to the middle section or you could continue down into the main tower.

02:34:16.332 --> 02:34:17.092
Unknown: Let's just go down.

02:34:17.652 --> 02:34:19.492
Seeker: There was nothing on that middle section aside from-

02:34:19.532 --> 02:34:19.532
DM: There's-

02:34:19.532 --> 02:34:20.352
Unknown: ... the two statues we killed

02:34:20.432 --> 02:34:21.712
Wellby: Yeah, nothing else out there.

02:34:21.712 --> 02:34:22.732
Delwath: I mean, we didn't search it.

02:34:22.752 --> 02:34:24.212
DM: Well, you haven't gone out there.

02:34:24.752 --> 02:34:25.512
Seeker: We saw it from the air.

02:34:25.572 --> 02:34:26.732
DM: You saw it from the air.

02:34:26.732 --> 02:34:28.392
Unknown: You wanna go out there? You wanna go out?

02:34:28.472 --> 02:34:30.212
Wellby: I don't like the idea of something being behind us.

02:34:30.212 --> 02:34:30.552
Unknown: Yeah, yeah, yeah, no.

02:34:30.592 --> 02:34:30.872
Wellby: So we don't.

02:34:30.912 --> 02:34:31.492
Unknown: Down.

02:34:31.512 --> 02:34:32.032
Seeker: Fair.

02:34:32.052 --> 02:34:32.052
DM: Yeah.

02:34:32.072 --> 02:34:32.852
Wellby: So I'll go out.

02:34:33.352 --> 02:34:33.452
Unknown: Yeah.

02:34:33.592 --> 02:34:35.892
Wellby: Maybe assist. We'll take a perceptive walk around.

02:34:36.712 --> 02:34:36.772
DM: Yeah.

02:34:36.772 --> 02:34:37.772
Wellby: See if there's anything else out there.

02:34:38.552 --> 02:34:41.192
DM: Okay. Um, make a perception check with advantage.

02:34:43.292 --> 02:34:44.872
Wellby: 19, 32.

02:34:45.732 --> 02:34:46.852
DM: Um, nothing.

02:34:46.852 --> 02:34:50.512
Wellby: [laughs] All right, I'm reasonably confident there's nothing there.

02:34:50.972 --> 02:34:50.992
DM: Yeah.

02:34:50.992 --> 02:34:52.011
Wellby: All right, cool. Down.

02:34:52.632 --> 02:34:53.832
Delwath: All right, onward.

02:34:53.832 --> 02:34:57.552
DM: Uh, you descend down, um, and you come...

02:34:59.452 --> 02:35:01.372
Kenzo: Weren't there four statues at the start of this thing?

02:35:01.372 --> 02:35:01.812
Unknown: Two.

02:35:01.812 --> 02:35:02.372
Wellby: There were only two, yeah.

02:35:02.432 --> 02:35:03.472
DM: Yeah, there was only ever two.

02:35:03.492 --> 02:35:03.752
Unknown: Okay.

02:35:05.132 --> 02:35:05.332
DM: Um,

02:35:06.512 --> 02:35:09.492
DM: you come down, um, into

02:35:10.912 --> 02:35:17.572
DM: a, the, the, the next room down of the tower is just one large open room.

02:35:17.572 --> 02:35:18.992
DM: There are stairs that continue down.

02:35:18.992 --> 02:35:22.272
DM: There's windows. There were no windows in the room at the very top.

02:35:22.272 --> 02:35:26.832
DM: The windows are open and you can smell the salt air of the sea blowing in.

02:35:26.832 --> 02:35:28.712
DM: You can hear the waves crashing.

02:35:28.732 --> 02:35:29.072
Wellby: That's suspicious.

02:35:29.072 --> 02:35:29.572
Unknown: Sounds pleasant.

02:35:30.172 --> 02:35:30.732
DM: Um.

02:35:30.732 --> 02:35:32.152
Unknown: [laughs]

02:35:32.252 --> 02:35:35.732
DM: Uh, there is almost nothing here.

02:35:35.732 --> 02:35:37.732
DM: Um, there are

02:35:39.072 --> 02:35:47.412
DM: perhaps once, like, a desk, but the wood, wood has over many, many years has almost entirely rotted away.

02:35:48.592 --> 02:35:49.992
DM: Um, there are,

02:35:52.292 --> 02:35:56.852
DM: uh, yeah, there's like dust on the floor where one might have

02:35:58.892 --> 02:35:59.732
DM: once had

02:36:01.132 --> 02:36:02.892
DM: shelves or chairs.

02:36:03.712 --> 02:36:06.372
DM: Um, there's stairs going further down.

02:36:06.892 --> 02:36:08.652
Wellby: Just everything is disintegrated.

02:36:08.652 --> 02:36:10.452
DM: Everything is disintegrated in this room.

02:36:10.972 --> 02:36:11.652
Kenzo: Nothing magical?

02:36:12.492 --> 02:36:13.012
DM: Nothing magical.

02:36:13.132 --> 02:36:14.492
Wellby: No disturbances in the dust.

02:36:16.392 --> 02:36:18.312
DM: Make a perception check.

02:36:19.272 --> 02:36:20.292
Wellby: Uh, 25.

02:36:21.092 --> 02:36:22.492
